  "question": {
    "text": "The natural number&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>, for which the coefficient of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> in the binomial expansion of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>22</mn></msup></math> is 1540,&nbsp;is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "13",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The general term in the binomial expansion,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mn>22</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msup></mfenced><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>22</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>For the coefficient of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>22</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>22</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>22</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>44</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>45</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>22</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>22</mn></mmultiscripts></math></p><p>So possible values&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>43</mn></math>, but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>22</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mn>1540</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></math></p>"
  }
